50	// --- where a declared pack's tasks live ---------------------------------------
51	
52	// A pack contributes tasks only if the repo DECLARES it: presence on disk is not
53	// activation (core's rule), and the mount carries packs a repo never declared. So
54	// the roster is built from the declaration list, and a task directory belonging to
55	// an undeclared pack is skipped rather than rendered greyed-out.
56	//
57	// Two roots, because the same code reads the canon home and a member: the home
58	// runs from the repo root (`packs/<id>`), a member from the mount
